Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:35:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1028/1177] Score check, MIDI out and in, section markers, one
 voice moved; a transposer fix

- heresy-abc.js ports YuE2 Studio abc_tools.py (Apache-2.0): the native two-voice dialect,
  read strictly to the sounding notes (counts checked equal to the Python on three takes).
  report(): key, BPM, meter, bars, time, sections; per voice notes, notes a minute, range,
  sounding share, chords; the Ins : Vocal ratio.
- Under the take score and the form score: the check (or the exact error, with group and
  bar), MIDI export (tempo, meters, keys, a track per voice, sections as markers), a marker
  CSV, MIDI import (one line per voice, 1/16 grid, spelled in the file key or a chosen one;
  read back through the parser), and one voice moved by scale steps in its key, its own
  inflections kept, chords and the other voice untouched (an octave down is exactly -12).
- heresy-transpose.js (1018): a note right after a rest (zd) was taken for part of a word
  and left where it was: 1 to 11 wrong notes a score. Now 0 of 2883 in 15 transpositions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
